1. INTRODUCTION
Fire accidents cause severe loss of life and property every year. Traditional fire alarm systems detect fire only after ignition. The proposed AI-Based Fire Prediction System (NeuroFlare) predicts fire risk before an outbreak using IoT sensors and Machine Learning algorithms.

1.a Objective
• To design a smart fire prediction system.
• To integrate IoT sensors with AI-based decision making.
• To reduce emergency response time.
• To send real-time alerts using buzzer and cloud notifications.
• To develop a low-cost and scalable safety solution.

1.b Materials Required
•	Hardware Components:
•	NodeMCU # ESP32
•	MQ-2 Smoke Sensor
•	MQ-135 Gas Sensor
•	DHT22 Temperature & Humidity Sensor
•	Flame Sensor
•	Buzzer 
•	LED Indicators
•	Jumper Wires
•	Breadboard
•	Software & Tools:
•	Arduino IDE
•	Arduino App Lab
•	Python for Machine Learning Model
•	ThingSpeak / Firebase Cloud Platform
•	Embedded C / C++
•	Serial Monitor (Debug & Test)
2. METHODOLOGY USED
Step 1: Sensors continuously collect temperature, humidity, smoke, and flame data.
Step 2: NodeMCU transmits data to the cloud using Wi-Fi.
Step 3: A Machine Learning model analyzes data and calculates fire probability.
Step 4: If probability exceeds threshold, buzzer activates and notification is sent.
Step 5: System continues real-time monitoring.

